---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const pageTitle = "About";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">About</h2>
  <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-4">
    <p>
      I'm working toward a B.S. in Computer Science at Colorado State University
      (expected May 2028), after earning an Associate of Science with Honors at
      Front Range Community College. Before that I completed Flatiron School's
      software engineering bootcamp.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm currently rebuilding A1 Wildwater's website in Astro as their
      part-time web developer. I've taught more than 300 STEM lessons in
      programming, game development and web development to students aged 8 to
      18, and I was a teaching assistant for Computer Architecture at Front
      Range.
    </p>
    <p>
      Away from the keyboard, I lead whitewater rafting trips with A1 Wildwater
      as a Wilderness First Responder and work as a sales specialist at REI. In
      my free time you'll find me on the slopes, caving with the Northern
      Colorado Grotto, or out on a mountain trail. I like hard problems for the
      same reason I like hard rapids: they're puzzles you solve one move at a
      time.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
